For me though it started with the launch of the Switch. There channel was special, but the day the Switch launched it all changed...or within a week or so of that.

&amp;#x200B;

That is when the content changed. They started covering games I have no interest in, and to be honest I can't watch about 90% of the videos because they aren't about anything that interests me. It's been like that since 2017.....Leading up to the Switch's launch was amazing....and then things changed.

&amp;#x200B;

It feels like they are coasting a bit now.

&amp;#x200B;

That being said, I still really like the channel, it's just not my go to channel. It used to be the first channel I clicked on every day, and sometimes I go 10-14 days without ever clicking on it....because I know most of the content won't interest me.

&amp;#x200B;

I hope in 2020 they can refocus on moving forward in a way that makes sense for how they used to be. It should be an exciting year so I'm expecting some quality discussion and videos from them, and truly wish them the best, I just think they can do a bit better.

